{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1072524-pierce-deception-and-mind-magic","id":1072524,"title":"Pierce Deception and Mind Magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-03T07:38:15-07:00","id":1072524,"title":"Pierce Deception and Mind Magic","content":"Hi wise ones. Would a testimony based on an false memory created by a Mind spell trigger Pierce Deception?.<br /> In example, I modify a witness memory to change the face of the guy who spoke with him 2 days ago. Later, that witness identifies the guy following his false memory. Would his statement trigger a nearby Pierce Deception?.<br /> It's easy to understand that lies are detected by the spell, but honest comunications based in false facts are much more shadowy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3008-masa","name":"Masa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3008_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T07:48:15-07:00","id":1072527,"title":"","content":"It wouldn't trigger Pierce Deception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T07:49:08-07:00","id":1072529,"title":"","content":"Gut feeling without checking the book is that the lie wouldn't, but a CoW might occur against the altered memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T07:57:49-07:00","id":1072536,"title":"","content":"When in doubt, go for Clash of Wills. <br /> <br /> Although I see an argument for Pierce Deception not working, because it specifically can't pierce lies not made in the moment, and technically you aren't lying if you have a faulty memory...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T08:04:55-07:00","id":1072542,"title":"","content":"It can detect lies &quot;not made in the moment&quot;, but it can't detect a liar when he isn't lying. For example of &quot;not made in the moment&quot; lie, look at the spell: it can tell you that dyed hair color is a &quot;lie&quot;. It's a Prime spell - I imagine it checks the &quot;truth&quot; presented by the liar against capital T &quot;Truth&quot; of the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T08:07:48-07:00","id":1072545,"title":"","content":"Yeah, WHW's more accurate. Should've chosen my words more carefully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T08:18:15-07:00","id":1072552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1072524-pierce-deception-and-mind-magic?p=1072542#post1072542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can detect lies &quot;not made in the moment&quot;, but it can't detect a liar when he isn't lying. For example of &quot;not made in the moment&quot; lie, look at the spell: it can tell you that dyed hair color is a &quot;lie&quot;. It's a Prime spell - I imagine it checks the &quot;truth&quot; presented by the liar against capital T &quot;Truth&quot; of the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point but, can detect when someone tells a lie because he thinks it's true?. Hell, he was sure it was the true!. In fact he is not lying, he just tells what he remembers even if it's nopt the &quot;Thruth&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3008-masa","name":"Masa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3008_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T08:35:30-07:00","id":1072556,"title":"","content":"I assume it doesn't care about what they think, because Words of Truth won't allow you to say something that you think it's true but it isn't true. Though they won't tell you if it's because your faith isn't strong enough, or if it's because you have a faulty information.<br /> This is not Mind Magic, remember; it doesn't perform a &quot;mind scan&quot; to check if the person in question is lying or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T15:20:29-07:00","id":1072724,"title":"","content":"I think context is important. <br /> It is a mind spell so it should be concerned with the state of the mind. <br /> So no the surpernal truth but the persons truth. <br /> So it will trigger when someone decided to lie. Even if the lie is fact or fiction. <br /> <br /> If it worked by surpernal truth it's the most powerful spell in the game. In a game where mages are trying to react the surpernal truth of the world and break away the shackles if the LIe. <br /> I could get my friend to state things and the spell would let me know the universal truth of the statement.Ames investigation plots easy. <br /> My friend could just say &quot;the butler is the killer&quot; and the spell will tell me if that statement is objectively true. <br /> <br /> Tl;dr The spell picks up on what a person beloved to be a lie<br /> So the chafing of memory would work as the person believes he is telling the truth","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T15:37:22-07:00","id":1072732,"title":"","content":"Except it's not a mind spell, it's a Prime spell, and Prime operates on supernal truths.<br /> Of course, specific wording is very important here. &quot;I remember seeing him do the deed&quot; will not register as untrue if the memory is changed. Ditto for &quot;I think he did it&quot;. But &quot;He did it!&quot; should ping it, unless each statement like this is translated into supernal &quot;I think he did it&quot; before being checked against the Truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 04-03-2017, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T17:12:23-07:00","id":1072787,"title":"","content":"These are my thoughts:<br /> <br /> Pierce Deception does not detect the Truth, but rather any falsehood. More than that, it must be an active falsehood. It is my interpretation that a person who truly believes something is not actively lying. However, in this case there is a testimony in which the subject is to describe the memory which is altered. Any statements based upon the memory would, in my opinion, not ring to pierce deception. However, recalling the actual memory verbally or a mage using mind in order to look at the memory itself would quickly reveal - after a clash of wills - that there was a falsehood there. In this case, the lies are not the statements that the witness is giving. Instead, the falsehood is the witnesses own memory.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T17:22:30-07:00","id":1072795,"title":"","content":"Honestly, if I had to guess, I'd say that Pierce Deception would detect the statement as false but wouldn't reveal the speaker to be a liar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T17:32:12-07:00","id":1072805,"title":"","content":"This is a question that has been asked much, and has not yet been adequately answered by the developers.<br /> It depends entirely on whether you consider Prime as being able to detect objective, or active lies.<br /> <br /> I run it as only being able to detect active lies, statements made in the belief of their falsehood.<br /> If you want to use Mind magic to manipulate your memories, so that you can step around this, you can.<br /> <br /> Very helpful if you want to get around someone truth detection Magic in a sticky situation.<br /> Less helpful if they scrutinise your magically modified memories and realise you're attempting to trick them.<br /> And given that Prime Sight can detect all brands of Awakened Magic? It's highly probable that they will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T15:09:31-07:00","id":1073389,"title":"","content":"I would fall back on a good old Clash of Wills. You have one spell designed to conceal the truth (whether the speaker is a willing participant or not) and another designed to burn through lies and detect the truth. If that then provokes the Prime User to investigate further..... isnt that the stuff plot hooks are made of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T17:21:07-07:00","id":1073446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1072524-pierce-deception-and-mind-magic?p=1073389#post1073389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would fall back on a good old Clash of Wills. You have one spell designed to conceal the truth (whether the speaker is a willing participant or not) and another designed to burn through lies and detect the truth. If that then provokes the Prime User to investigate further..... isnt that the stuff plot hooks are made of?</div> </div> </div> </div>So basically, damned if you do, damned if you don't? The options I see with that are:<br /> 1. Prime user wins CoW, sees the truth, you're in deep shit for lying to them with Magic<br /> 2. Prime user loses CoW, doesn't see the truth, realises you contested his Truth detection spell, now he's on your case, likely not what you wanted when you were lying<br /> <br /> With that, you just can't win, and Prime 1 renders all attempts at subterfuge entirely pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T17:41:23-07:00","id":1073458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1072524-pierce-deception-and-mind-magic?p=1073446#post1073446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> With that, you just can't win, and Prime 1 renders all attempts at subterfuge entirely pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to the Mage. A lot of conventional plot structures go right trough the window.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T17:47:56-07:00","id":1073459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1072524-pierce-deception-and-mind-magic?p=1073446#post1073446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So basically, damned if you do, damned if you don't? The options I see with that are:<br /> 1. Prime user wins CoW, sees the truth, you're in deep shit for lying to them with Magic<br /> 2. Prime user loses CoW, doesn't see the truth, realises you contested his Truth detection spell, <b>now he's on your case</b>, likely not what you wanted when you were lying</div> </div> </div> </div>All the Prime mage knows is that the Mind mage doesn't want other mages probing his mind around. Which is understandable when you're a mage. And most people don't take kindly to other people trying to verify every single one of their statements, or taking every one of their decisions to court so that it can be legally justified. Especially considering the people you're talking to frequently maintain shadow identities and secret conspiracies, making the old &quot;But you wouldn't lie if you had nothing to hide!&quot; claim a simplistic and naive approach.<br /> <br /> Heck, the Prime mage can't even be sure if the guy in front of him is really the one who put that mind shield in the first place. He might as well be a victim of a mind-clouding spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With that, you just can't win, and Prime 1 renders all attempts at subterfuge <b>entirely pointless</b>. </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't be quite so sure about this either. Saying Prime renders all subterfuge useless is like saying DNA tests and fingerprint tests render all false identities useless. Sure, you can get a sample from the other guy and run the test. But you don't usually take DNA samples from people you've just met or have absolutely no reason to suspect in the first place, at least in a polite society. And consilium politics are poltie indeed, since civility and MAD is largely what keeps mages from killing each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T17:53:30-07:00","id":1073464,"title":"","content":"I get what your saying, but 'all attempts at subterfuge' strikes me as somewhat hyperbolic. Prime 1 is the smallest problem for the scheme mentioned in the OP's scenario. If my Obrimos character walks up to the guy with the memory altering spell on him, my Peripheral Mage Sight will immediately tell me that the guy has an active spell on him. The Active Mage Sight I will almost immediately turn on should reveal the memory altering spell. Now its just a matter of time and spellwork to work out whats been altered, for which Pierce Deception might be useful with clever questioning, but calling in someone with the power to dispel it would probably be faster.<br /> <br /> I have this mental ruleshack I might use at my table, where CoW's where a Veiling spell wins don't let the opposing party realise their spell clashed, but I haven't really worked out all the implications.<br /> <br /> Edit: I had this whole thing planned where I said much the same stuff as 21C Hermit, but he was much more eloquent so I got rid of it. Whats left is just something addressing the OP's original question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6230,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","user":"Katana1515","date":".  Praising 21C Hermit 04-04-2017, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T17:57:34-07:00","id":1073470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1072524-pierce-deception-and-mind-magic?p=1073464#post1073464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">my Peripheral Mage Sight will immediately tell me that the guy has an active spell on him</div> </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't.<br /> It only triggers to activated effects, not those that are currently already up an running.<br /> In addition if you want subterfuge in detecting spells, add in Prime 2 and your spells can't be passively seen in Active Mage Sight.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T19:10:23-07:00","id":1073493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1072524-pierce-deception-and-mind-magic?p=1073470#post1073470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It wouldn't.<br /> It only triggers to activated effects, not those that are currently already up an running.<br /> In addition if you want subterfuge in detecting spells, add in Prime 2 and your spells can't be passively seen in Active Mage Sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it detects <i>all</i> active spells, not just spells as they are activated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T19:22:55-07:00","id":1073502,"title":"","content":"Embellishing a bit further on what I said earlier.<br /> <br /> The thing is, Pierce Deception does not detect things that are wrong - just lies, illusions, and phantasms (active at that). In this case, it depends on what the character is looking at. Is the character utilizing Pierce Deception listening to the testimony, or examining the memory?<br /> <br /> If he's listening to the testimony, he's not listening to a lie. The fact that the memory is changed does not make his words or statements a lie. It simply makes what he is using to base his statement wrong. It is as much a lie to say that a person committed a crime due to your memories as it is to state that someone committed a crime due to seeing that person under a manyfaces spell. At the end of the day - the lie, the illusion, is not the testimony - it's the memories that lie and deceive.<br /> <br /> If however he examines the memory, he would recieve a clash of wills and, upon winning, be able to determine that the memory was altered or that memories were missing. Upon failing the clash, he would be able to tell something was wrong with the memory but be unable to determine exactly what.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T19:52:06-07:00","id":1073515,"title":"","content":"How do you combine that definition of what a lie is with the fact that this spell literally triggers when your mom walks in and asks &quot;how do I look today?&quot;, and Pierce Deception is going off the charts while pointing a big arrow at her hair color, because she decided that she always wanted to be a redhead? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This spell only reveals \u201cactive\u201d untruths: the subject would see that <br /> someone with dyed hair isn\u2019t really a blonde, or recognize a lie when <br /> she heard it, but she wouldn\u2019t know that a Wall Street executive has <br /> been committing tax fraud for years just by looking at him. If she got a <br /> look at his tax return, however, she would see that it was a falsehood. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T20:37:51-07:00","id":1073538,"title":"","content":"The hair change is an active illusion. You can perceive her hair, look at it yourself, and know that that is not it's natural state.<br /> <br /> Taking the dyed hair concept: Looking at someone, you immediately can tell if they dyed their hair or not - but say your looking at the picture created by an artist rather than the actual person themselves. The artist drew that person with the hair color she puts out. The artist does not recognize that the hair is dyed, and when he expresses that he assumes that the hair color is what the hair color is. You would not immediately know that the hair was dyed looking at this picture - you would have to look at the woman herself to be able to tell that her hair was natural, dyed, or she put on a wig.<br /> <br /> In the same regards, a person giving a testimony assumes his testimony is the truth - he does not doubt his memories, even though his memories are false - so the words he gives to convey and express his memories do not ring as false because you are not looking at his memories, but hearing his honest perception of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T00:43:38-07:00","id":1073611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1072524-pierce-deception-and-mind-magic?p=1073446#post1073446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So basically, damned if you do, damned if you don't? The options I see with that are:<br /> 1. Prime user wins CoW, sees the truth, you're in deep shit for lying to them with Magic<br /> 2. Prime user loses CoW, doesn't see the truth, realises you contested his Truth detection spell, now he's on your case, likely not what you wanted when you were lying<br /> <br /> With that, you just can't win, and Prime 1 renders all attempts at subterfuge entirely pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Something about Clashes of Will, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T08:39:44-07:00","id":1073737,"title":"","content":"I would also say clash of wills. The mind spell prevents the liar from realizing he's lying, but Pierce Deception generally doesn't care about what a person thinks- it's prime, and thus concerned with the truth. A person who is repeating a mundane lie he believes is true is caught by Pierce Deception- (as much false advertisement rings untrue, even if the person designing the ad believes otherwise- whether through wishful thinking or being fooled by someone else). However, the magical weight behind the deception (the Memory Hole spell) mean's it's a magical lie, and thus subject to a clash of wills.<br /> <br /> Of course, it's fairly moot anyway. Prime Mage sight spots awakened magic, so unless the mage has prime herself to conceal the spell, an mage with prime will be able to spot the existence of the memory-modifying spell, and probably figure out what it is.<br /> <br /> I'm of the firm opinion that Pierce Deception should be able to detect unwitting or sincerely-held lies, for a couple of reasons. One, it differentiates it more strongly from Mind magic that does the same thing. Two, Prime, being truth and not mind, should care about cosmic rightness, not subjective opinion; and it fits the Obirimos path to care about external cosmic rightness as well. Three, it fits the <i>holy shit</i> feel of Obirimos magic. Fourth, it gives an excuse for Obirimos to listen to cult leaders, crazy street preachers, conspiracy theorists, crank (and not so crank) science articles, and other odd or dubious sources, just to see if there's something there. I find this can be a great source of plot hooks and mystery; if the lunatic says aliens have infiltrated the IRS and Pierce deception comes back &quot;True&quot;, well, that's plot hook right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8045-azunth","name":"Azunth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T09:09:00-07:00","id":1073751,"title":"","content":"Yeah, imagine going for a walk with this thing on, being assaulted by lies from every angle, and finding something really weird to ring true in contrast to everything else. Because let's be honest, this spell will turn you insane if you try to experience everyday life with it. LIES, LIES ALL AROUND.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T09:40:03-07:00","id":1073771,"title":"","content":"I personally find it a bit weird that it's one the Mage casts on himself rather than on a subject, that would clear the problem right up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 04-05-2017, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T12:53:47-07:00","id":1073840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azunth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1072524-pierce-deception-and-mind-magic?p=1073737#post1073737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also say clash of wills. The mind spell prevents the liar from realizing he's lying, but Pierce Deception generally doesn't care about what a person thinks- it's prime, and thus concerned with the truth. A person who is repeating a mundane lie he believes is true is caught by Pierce Deception- (as much false advertisement rings untrue, even if the person designing the ad believes otherwise- whether through wishful thinking or being fooled by someone else). However, the magical weight behind the deception (the Memory Hole spell) mean's it's a magical lie, and thus subject to a clash of wills.<br /> <br /> Of course, it's fairly moot anyway. Prime Mage sight spots awakened magic, so unless the mage has prime herself to conceal the spell, an mage with prime will be able to spot the existence of the memory-modifying spell, and probably figure out what it is.<br /> <br /> I'm of the firm opinion that Pierce Deception should be able to detect unwitting or sincerely-held lies, for a couple of reasons. One, it differentiates it more strongly from Mind magic that does the same thing. Two, Prime, being truth and not mind, should care about cosmic rightness, not subjective opinion; and it fits the Obirimos path to care about external cosmic rightness as well. Three, it fits the <i>holy shit</i> feel of Obirimos magic. Fourth, it gives an excuse for Obirimos to listen to cult leaders, crazy street preachers, conspiracy theorists, crank (and not so crank) science articles, and other odd or dubious sources, just to see if there's something there. I find this can be a great source of plot hooks and mystery; if the lunatic says aliens have infiltrated the IRS and Pierce deception comes back &quot;True&quot;, well, that's plot hook right there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I'd classify that viewpoint as detecting active lies. I mean, a lot of those I would consider active lies (false advertising, for instance), but some of those could be true and still come up as lies. Aliens could have infiltrated the IRS, but if I make up a statement saying that aliens have infiltrated the IRS to grab attention, it doesn't matter that that's true - at the end of the day I'm lying about the fact.<br /> <br /> It also cuts out a lot of Mystery (capital A) when you apply the lack of activeness required to make such a lie. &quot;God exists&quot; (Ping). Welp, guess not (or, God does not - game depending). The first vampire was longinus (Ping) Welp, sorry my Lance friend. Atlantis was real (Ping!) - no point of debate required (even though this was toned down a lot <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)! I'm of the mind that subjectiveness is an important factor in the spell. A lie is defined as an intentionally false statement - keyword being intentional.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1072524-pierce-deception-and-mind-magic?p=1073751#post1073751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, imagine going for a walk with this thing on, being assaulted by lies from every angle, and finding something really weird to ring true in contrast to everything else. Because let's be honest, this spell will turn you insane if you try to experience everyday life with it. LIES, LIES ALL AROUND.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure about insane. Jaded, perhaps, but not insane. Suddenly you become Doctor House, stating everyone lies :-p","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T18:37:00-07:00","id":1073960,"title":"","content":"The intention matters people have won me over, though I'll be very relaxed with the level of intention required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T07:01:50-07:00","id":1074637,"title":"","content":"It works on &quot;active lies,&quot; which implies willful deceit. Prime 1 only registers if the subject is deliberately lying. It cant be checking &quot;does this match its suoernal representation?&quot; Because then it would always ping because the abyss is a thing.<br /> <br /> Far more importantly, it being able to dstect untruths to that degree means that any Mage with Prime 1 can confirm or deny any theory by just saying what they think the solution of the plot is... ... amd with Reach they can make doe eyes at the Storyteller, who is obligated to tell them the plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T08:36:47-07:00","id":1074670,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1157\" data-vbnamecard=\"1157\">SoulGambit</a> No, the ST is required to do no such thing since information revealed is via &quot;symbols&quot;, it might give a hint, but it can still be very cryptic. Also a plot doesn't inherently require deception on any level so that's also just a flat out wrong assumption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T22:03:53-07:00","id":1074994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrownedSun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1072524-pierce-deception-and-mind-magic?p=1073960#post1073960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The intention matters people have won me over, though I'll be very relaxed with the level of intention required.</div> </div> </div> </div>The lie <i>is</i> active in the example raised: The mind spell is lying to the witness. His memory is lying to him because of it. The witness is <i>repeating the lie</i>.<br /> &quot;Active&quot; is in quotes because the lie needs to be applicable and present to the witness for the spell to trigger. You have to <b>see the lie</b> in the tax returns, for example, or the wrong colored hair. They don't require intent to deceive. A hair job really doesn't qualify as active deception in the sense being claimed here.<br /> <br /> (well, maybe if the hairdresser said &quot;Oh, you look <i>good</i>.&quot; or something)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T22:31:44-07:00","id":1075008,"title":"","content":"The reason the dyed hair comes up is because dyed hair is an illusion - an active illusion that you can see. Your immediate perception is that that is their hair color, because they made that their hair color. But it's fake, its false, and the real hair color is a different hair color that they -changed- their hair color to, and the evidence is right there in front of you. There is deception there - it's just not malicious deception in the sense that telling a lie usually is.<br /> <br /> In this example, you do not witness the lie - because the statement itself is not a lie, the memory is. Now - it may be up to you as a storyteller to decide if recounting a memory qualifies as 'witnessing' that memory to be able to deduce that there was a falsehood. But if you did qualify that the recounting qualified as witnessing the memory, you would not be detecting that the witnesses statement was false - you would be detecting that their -memory- was false. This is an important distinction, because it tells you whether or not the witness themselves it the one giving the false testimony or not. I, personally, would not count someone recalling a memory as me witnessing their memory enough for Pierce Deception to work. In order to deduce the memory as a falsehood, I would actually need a tool to look at the memory - such as telepathy. YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}